{"recordKind":"informed-prospective-P-scientific-review-candidate","recordId":"sn-own-indicator-P1-informed-A-20261017-v1","reviewerRole":"independent A; informed followup","goalId":"d2ccd1d5-56f7-583f-9724-e97441367f91","verdict":"P1_KEEP_PROFILE_EXACT_PROSPECTIVE_MACHINE_CANDIDATE","evidenceLevel":"E1","maximumClaimScope":"G1","FIRST":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-SN-own-indicator-P1-source66-informed-independent-a-v1/FIRST.SN-own-indicator-P1-and-source66.scientific-findings.sealed.json","sha256":"a86c10d3bbb267931020b43280653639c5a9151e7a579b950171129370360ae7","bytes":27867},"inputProfile":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-SN-indicator-P1-native1-root-v2/capsule/curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-17/chemie-current439-SN-indicator-P1-native1-root-v2/science/candidate/P1.successor.whole-profile.body.json","sha256":"a19098b63a322d3faa8bbfcf82bdede135b2891796aad12de4c8c2755ba10a4c","bytes":16958},"inputCurrentPRecord":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-SN-indicator-P1-native1-root-v2/capsule/curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-17/chemie-current439-SN-indicator-P1-native1-root-v2/P1.current-SN-indicator.author-candidate.jsonl","sha256":"676c9d2f5ea3782723b202b4c26087f5301166eab87d6b030fc33ce8e61de0c5","bytes":18181},"findings":[{"id":"P-A01","decision":"accepted","topic":"Own physical operator and raw evidence","reason":"Both cases require the learner personally to take separate coded aliquots, use fresh indicators, follow the product-specific exposure/read procedure and record their own colours, conditions and control before interpretation or key disclosure. Teacher witnessing and original raw fields distinguish personal execution from copied colours, chart discussion or teacher demonstration. The blank template is explicitly unperformed and all learner observations remain null."},{"id":"P-A02","decision":"accepted","topic":"Defined materials and executable procedures","reason":"The contract identifies exact ready-made colourless P712 citrate-buffer pH4 and 9977 phosphate-buffer pH7 products, exact teacher-only NaHCO3 and anhydrous citric-acid source substances and final concentrations, original 92110 and 90201 products, clean dedicated transfer apparatus, labelled vessels/forceps/catch tray, sample supply and lighting/temperature. At least20mL per sample plus separate control, and teacher-selected small tubes whose brim volume fits the supply, make the two procedures executable without requiring an invented indicator recipe or a nonexistent universal colour chart."},{"id":"P-A03","decision":"accepted","topic":"Product-specific primary fidelity","reason":"92110 all-field approximately1s exposure, excess removal and comparison with its original chart, including the insufficient-buffering exception, agree with the manufacturer instruction. For 90201, damp reading with its own scale and the weak-buffer procedure against the inner tube wall, filled to the brim and read through glass after about1minute, agree with the actual linked manufacturer instruction. No liquid-indicator drop-count recipe is invented. References and outcomes remain conditional on actual stock, colour matching and conditions."},{"id":"P-A04","decision":"accepted","topic":"Control, classification and meaningful new transfer","reason":"Each case uses an independently observed known 9977 pH7 control under that case procedure; this checks method/chart behaviour without pretending to calibrate all pH values. Three clear samples in each case can distinguish acidic/approximately neutral/alkaline. New citric acid replaces the first citrate-buffer sample and 90201 paper, chart and reading method replace 92110, requiring fresh physical evidence and a reason why old field patterns cannot be copied. This is meaningful transfer, not merely recoding."},{"id":"P-A05","decision":"accepted","topic":"Chemical plausibility and precision limits","reason":"Teacher NaHCO3 8.40g/L is approximately0.100mol/L and an amphiprotic bicarbonate solution plausibly lies near pH8.3; the stated8-9 reference is broad rather than a measurement. Citric acid1.00g/L is approximately0.0052mol/L and plausibly acidic near pH2.8, within the stated2-4 reference. Ready-made pH4 and pH7 buffers are nominal20°C references. Paper matching gives approximate support only: near-neutral ambiguity, unstable or unmatchable colours leave classification/practical evidence open. Supplier buffer precision does not become strip-reading precision or proof of exact neutrality."},{"id":"P-A06","decision":"accepted","topic":"Limits before school execution","reason":"Exact stock, lot, expiry, original current comparison charts, current local supplier safety information, actual teacher preparation, room/age/PPE/vessel suitability, preflight distinguishability and explicit local release are required before learner use. Students do not weigh solids or prepare these solutions. No home test, tasting, mouth pipetting, sample mixing or improvised disposal is authorised. Teacher preflight is a stated future readiness check, not performed evidence. These execution conditions do not themselves leave a missing authoring fact in this prospective contract, and absence of a human trial alone is not a machine-P blocker."},{"id":"P-A07","decision":"accepted with bounded context observation","topic":"Goal and retained image use","reason":"The current goal covers suitable school experiments, the indicator actually used, classification and rough pH ranges; the two cases and rubric assess exactly that breadth. The retained red/green/blue cartoon with pH<7/=7/>7 is an introductory schematic. The contract explicitly disallows it as either actual original colour chart, mandatory colour sequence or raw experimental result. No image change is scientifically needed for this bounded P assessment; this is not D/page or V reapproval."}],"prerequisiteContextObservation":{"decision":"Whole1351706f and whole416dfd33 are not necessary prior competencies for these actual new cases; contextual13d4f336 safety application remains required before handling.","1351706f":"The whole competency is learner preparation of a homogeneous solution with documented work. Here the teacher supplies all ready-made/prepared solutions and handles solids, so that prior whole performance is not needed.","416dfd33":"After reading its whole current P, all e1-e4 are required there: taring/weighing, measurement, filtration/settling/decanting, original volumes/losses and clarity-versus-purity/recovery reasoning. None of those full weighing/separation/recovery routines is required to perform these indicator cases. Only narrow transfer, labelling, suitable tube/forceps handling and immediate own observation recording are needed, and may be introduced and rehearsed within this supervised indicator task. Familiarity is useful; it does not justify the whole416 prerequisite.","13d4f336":"The current full safety competency and P address actual eye protection, clear labelled workspace, rejecting an unknown vessel and immediate stop/report/local response to a splash or contamination. Those situations can occur with the actual aliquot and brim-fill actions. Its contextual safe application is therefore substantively necessary before handling, including teacher/local first-aid directions. This does not require chemistry preparation, filtration or weighing and cannot be discarded because its current requires link leads to a broader methods competency.","qualification":"This corrects the earlier provisional shorthand that general laboratory methods416 as a whole were needed. It is a P/material-context observation only: no edge deletion/addition, effective prerequisite/DAG validation, D binding acceptance or blanket P13d4/P416 reapproval."},"authoritativeApproval":false,"performedPracticalEvidence":false,"humanApproval":false,"DReviewPerformed":false}
{"recordKind":"informed-bounded-source-cell-qualification-review-candidate","recordId":"sn-source66-left-right-informed-A-20261017-v1","reviewerRole":"independent A; informed followup","sourceGoalId":"sn-chem-seki-sn-ch-klassenstufe-8-lb5-035-01-d0f98a3c","sourceGoalIndex":66,"verdict":"ACCEPT_BOUNDED_LEFT_RIGHT_QUALIFICATION_CANDIDATE","evidenceLevel":"E1","maximumClaimScope":"G1","FIRST":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-SN-own-indicator-P1-source66-informed-independent-a-v1/FIRST.SN-own-indicator-P1-and-source66.scientific-findings.sealed.json","sha256":"a86c10d3bbb267931020b43280653639c5a9151e7a579b950171129370360ae7","bytes":27867},"sourceCandidate":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-SN-left-right-source-cell-author-root-v1/candidate/DE_SN_CHEMIE_SEKI_LEHRPLAN_GYMNASIUM_2025.source-extraction.ONE-CELL-PENDING.left-right-v1.json","sha256":"375619ba4da73f535fc74df893ef5eb74713b2fa815397ae1bd2a70abafa09ed","bytes":400021},"originalPrimary":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-SN-indicator-own-investigation-P-author-successor-v1/archive/lehrplan-gymnasium-chemie-sachsen-2025.pdf","sha256":"3a74886e7ee9492b003d4916719e2b4644aef5fdfe8331cdefd8151fe0e86051","bytes":824141},"findings":[{"id":"S-A01","decision":"accepted","fields":["sourceText","parentBulletText","description","sourceTextKind","parentBulletTextKind","originalSourceCellLayout.leftColumnOriginalFragments"],"reason":"The actual left cell contains the introductory insight into everyday importance/use/handling of acids and their acidic solutions, plus its indented experimental investigation of acidic solutions with indicators. The candidate retains both left components and the original distinction between insight and experimental action; its authored paraphrase does not upgrade insight to an additional stronger operator. The parent field retains the parent alone."},{"id":"S-A02","decision":"accepted","fields":["originalSourceCellLayout.rightColumnGuidance","originalSourceCellLayout.rightColumnCrossCurricularReferences","originalSourceCellLayout.rightColumnSEMarker"],"reason":"The physical two-column page places acid classification, oxygen-containing inorganic acids, behaviour rules and acid-rain examples in the right remarks column, alongside responsibility/sustainability references. The introductory curriculum rules assign remarks recommendation character. The candidate correctly separates them from additional universally mandatory left-column duties. SE is aligned with the indented investigation and does not make that left experimental operator optional; investigation cannot be replaced by supplied colours. This local column qualification does not waive safety duties from other sources or local lab rules."},{"id":"S-A03","decision":"accepted","fields":["rawSourceText","rawSourceSpan","rawParentBulletText","passages[LB5].text","passages[LB5].metadata.currentSourceCellQualification"],"reason":"The old merged text is openly retained as historical authored extraction and the unchanged passage explicitly labels itself a nonliteral editorial summary. New metadata points to the selected current left/right cell qualification, so those merged words must not be used to invent further mandatory operators. Remaining raw historical wording is not a substantive current source-meaning defect under that explicit authority distinction."},{"id":"S-A04","decision":"accepted bounded qualification only","fields":["courseLevel","tags","originalSourceCellLayout.currentLearnerExecutionProven"],"reason":"This is grade8 SekI source context. Existing GK_LK is a compatibility projection label, not a claim that Saxony offers upper-secondary course levels in grade8. Source text fidelity and prospective experimental opportunity do not establish actual learner performance or accepted canonical mappings."}],"sourceUnionVerdict":"OPEN","canonicalMappingAcceptance":false,"performedPracticalEvidence":false,"humanApproval":false,"DReviewPerformed":false}
